Constructors
- Constructors are a special method that are invoked in the main method to create an object (Circle circ = **new Circle()**)
- Mainly designed to initialize data members
- No-argument constructors set default values for data members
- ^^(A class has a default constructor only if the class does not define any constructor)
- Convenience constructors set specified values that is called from *this* keyword
- A constructor must have the same name as the class itself
- Constructors do not have a return type or a void keyword(otherwise, it would be a method)
- Convenience constructors can be overloaded(multiple constructors with the same name, diff signature)
- you can add print statements inside constructors and it will print when you create a new object
- you can copy an array in a constructor or use "copy constructor" to copy objects 
- String object types and static member initialization recommended not in constructor


