Variables of primitive types vs reference types
- A variable of a primitive type holds a value of the primitive type
- A variable of a reference type holds a reference to where an object is stored in memory

int i = 1; // Primitive type
Circle c; //Reference type

- When an object is no longer referenced, it is considered "garbage collection", which removes objects in memory that are no longer able to be accessed

