***Visibility modifiers***
- Public: classes methods and data fields are denoted to be accessed by any class
- Private: opposite of public; only keeps to its class
- Default: same as public but package secure 
- Protected

Data field encapsulation(getters and setters)
- Modifying data fields directly is not good practice for two reasons:
	1. Data could be tampered
	2. Class becomes difficult to maintain and vulnerable to bugs
	
- To fix those reasons, data fields can be declared private(data field encapsulation)
- now that data fields are private, they cannot be accessed outside the class and must be invoked some other way hmm i wonder
- getter method(accessor): returns a value
- setter method(mutator): sets a new value

